            "left_title": "Beginner Hula Hoop Trick: Hooping in Lasso",
            "left_heading_tag": "h3",
            "left_description": "<p>Hooping in Lasso is a foundational skill that involves spinning the hoop around your hand above your head.</p>",
            "left_custom_block_padding": "50px 20px 50px 20px",
            "left_enable_custom_text_color": false,
            "left_custom_text_color": "rgba(0,0,0,0)",
            "left_enable_custom_link_color": false,
            "left_custom_link_color": "rgba(0,0,0,0)",
            "left_video_url": "https://youtu.be/yb1RxojqcZU",
            "left_content_alignment": "top-left",
            "left_background_color": "rgba(0,0,0,0)",
            "right_title": "",
            "right_heading_tag": "h3",
            "right_description": "<ol><li>Begin by grabbing your hoop at the top middle point with an under hand hold. Use your left hand. </li><li>Place the hoop to your left side.</li><li> Carry the hoop across your body and upwards into a Lasso Position. </li><li>As the hoop comes up above your head, release your grip to let it move freely around the palm of your hand between your thumb and finger tips. </li><li>Gently rotate your hand slightly to maintain motion.</li></ol>",
            "right_custom_block_padding": "50px 20px 50px 20px",
