            "background_image_size": "cover",
            "section_margin": 50,
            "min_height": 200,
            "left_title": "Intermediate Hula Hoop Trick: The Vortex",
            "left_heading_tag": "h3",
            "left_description": "<p>The Vortex is a continuous lasso while standing inside the hoop. It is important to know lasso before trying this trick.</p>",
            "left_custom_block_padding": "50px 20px 50px 20px",
            "left_enable_custom_text_color": false,
            "left_custom_text_color": "rgba(0,0,0,0)",
            "left_enable_custom_link_color": false,
            "left_custom_link_color": "rgba(0,0,0,0)",
            "left_video_url": "https://youtu.be/B7HlNLJ4VGU",
            "left_content_alignment": "top-left",
            "left_background_color": "rgba(0,0,0,0)",
            "right_title": "",
            "right_heading_tag": "h3",
            "right_description": "<ol><li>Enter the vortex through either lasso position or your waste.</li><li>While hooping, place your hand on the center of your back and grab the hoop.</li><li>Bring your hand up and the hoop rotates and pass it to the back of your other hand.</li><li>With the hoop above you, allow it to rotate around to your palm to grab it.</li><li>As you lower the hoop, catch it with the other hand behind your body and repeat.</li></ol>",
            "right_custom_block_padding": "50px 20px 50px 20px",
            "right_enable_custom_text_color": false,
            "right_custom_text_color": "rgba(0,0,0,0)",
