        "video_two_col_YJ6BDj": {
          "type": "video_two_col",
          "settings": {
            "block_background_type": "color",
            "section_bg_color": "rgba(0,0,0,0)",
            "overlay_opacity": 0,
            "background_image_size": "cover",
            "section_margin": 50,
            "min_height": 200,
            "left_title": "Advanced Hula Hoop Trick: Foot to Neck Transfer",
            "left_heading_tag": "h3",
            "left_description": "<p>Foot to Neck Transfer involves sitting up into the hoop and transferring it from your foot to neck.</p>",
            "left_custom_block_padding": "50px 20px 50px 20px",
            "left_enable_custom_text_color": true,
            "left_custom_text_color": "#000000",
            "left_enable_custom_link_color": false,
            "left_custom_link_color": "rgba(0,0,0,0)",
            "left_video_url": "https://youtu.be/wQ5X4sH4tjg",
            "left_content_alignment": "top-left",
            "left_background_color": "rgba(0,0,0,0)",
            "right_title": "",
            "right_heading_tag": "h3",
            "right_description": "<ol><li>Begin by laying on your back while foot hooping. </li><li>When the hoop is spun so the hole of the hoop is above your head, quickly sit up. Simultaneously push your hooping foot forward.</li><li>When the hoop is at the top half of your foot and has gone half way around, bend your leg and pull the hoop downwards towards your head. </li><li>Move your head slightly to the side and duck into the hoop while also sliding your foot out in the direction the hoop is spinning. </li><li>Once the hoop is on your neck, lift your chin and sit up straight. </li><li>Continue neck hooping.</li></ol>",
            "right_custom_block_padding": "50px 20px 50px 20px",
            "right_enable_custom_text_color": true,
            "right_custom_text_color": "#000000",
            "right_enable_custom_link_color": false,
